138 63 218 0 224-182 406-407 406-224 0-406-182-406-406s183-406 407-406c80 0 155 22 218 62l250-250 125 125z m-812 250l0 438 437 0 0-438-437 0z m62 375l313 0 0-312-313 0 0 312z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Pan" data-attr="dragmode" data-val="pan" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m1000 350l-187 188 0-125-250 0 0 250 125 0-188 187-187-187 125 0 0-250-250 0 0 125-188-188 186-187 0 125 252 0 0-250-125 0 187-188 188 188-125 0 0 250 250 0 0-126 187 188z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom in" data-attr="zoom" data-val="in" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m1 787l0-875 875 0 0 875-875 0z m687-500l-187 0 0-187-125 0 0 187-188 0 0 125 188 0 0 187 125 0 0-187 187 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom out" data-attr="zoom" data-val="out" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m0 788l0-876 875 0 0 876-875 0z m688-500l-500 0 0 125 500 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Autoscale" data-attr="zoom" data-val="auto" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m250 850l-187 0-63 0 0-62 0-188 63 0 0 188 187 0 0 62z m688 0l-188 0 0-62 188 0 0-188 62 0 0 188 0 62-62 0z m-875-938l0 188-63 0 0-188 0-62 63 0 187 0 0 62-187 0z m875 188l0-188-188 0 0-62 188 0 62 0 0 62 0 188-62 0z m-125 188l-1 0-93-94-156 156 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Toggle Spike Lines" data-attr="_cartesianSpikesEnabled" data-val="on" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M512 409c0-57-46-104-103-104-57 0-104 47-104 104 0 57 47 103 104 103 57 0 103-46 103-103z m-327-39l92 0 0 92-92 0z m-185 0l92 0 0 92-92 0z m370-186l92 0 0 93-92 0z m0-184l92 0 0 92-92 0z" transform="matrix(1.5 0 0 -1.5 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in New Window" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="535" height="295"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><text class="draggable" name="text" x="204" y="132" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 204 132)" style="fill: rgb(0, 42, 255); font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; font-family: normal;">in</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="338" y="142" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 338 142)" style="fill: rgb(255, 0, 89); font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; font-family: bold;">out</text><g transform="translate(503,49)" x="503" y="49" title="codeHTML" width="497" height="621" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="222" height="200" style="height: 621px; width: 828.333px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 60%; height: 621px; width: 828.333px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
    
    &lt;h1&gt;Astable Multivibrator (Relaxation Oscillator) - SPICE Time Domain Analysis&lt;/h1&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Op-Amp:&lt;/strong&gt; TL084 (operational amplifier)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R1:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 kΩ (feedback resistor to inverting input)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R2:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 kΩ (positive feedback resistor)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R3:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 kΩ (reference resistor to ground)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C1:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 μF (timing capacitor)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V1:&lt;/strong&gt; +10V (positive supply)&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V2:&lt;/strong&gt; -10V (negative supply)&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;Oscillation Frequency Calculation&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
        β = R3 / (R2 + R3) = 1k / (1k + 1k) = 0.5&lt;br&gt;
        Threshold voltages: Vth+ = +5V, Vth- = -5V&lt;br&gt;
        T = 2RC × ln((1+β)/(1-β)) = 2 × 1k × 1μF × ln(3) ≈ &lt;strong&gt;2.2 ms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
        f = 1/T ≈ &lt;strong&gt;455 Hz&lt;/strong&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;Simulation Results&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;

        &lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3&gt;Capacitor Voltage V(in) - Blue&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;ul&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Exponential charging/discharging waveform&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Oscillates between approximately -4V and +4V&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Charges toward +10V when output is HIGH&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Discharges toward -10V when output is LOW&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Switches direction at ±5V thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

        &lt;div class=&quot;ch-col red&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3&gt;Output Voltage V(out) - Red&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;ul&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Square wave oscillating between +10V and -10V&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Period ≈ 2.2 ms (frequency ≈ 455 Hz)&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;50% duty cycle (symmetric oscillation)&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Switches when capacitor voltage reaches thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;Rail-to-rail output swing&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;ch-card green-border&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h2&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
        &lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;&gt;This circuit is an &lt;strong&gt;Astable Multivibrator&lt;/strong&gt; (Relaxation Oscillator) using a TL084 op-amp. The circuit generates continuous oscillation without any external input signal. The capacitor C1 charges and discharges through R1, while the positive feedback network (R2, R3) creates two threshold voltages at ±5V. When the capacitor voltage reaches +5V, the output switches from +10V to -10V, causing the capacitor to discharge. When it reaches -5V, the output switches back to +10V, and the cycle repeats. This creates a self-sustaining oscillation at approximately 455 Hz, producing both a square wave output and a triangular/exponential waveform at the capacitor.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot; style=&quot;background-color: #e8f8f5; border-left: 4px solid #1abc9c;&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h2 style=&quot;color: #16a085;&quot;&gt;Operating Principle&lt;/h2&gt;
        &lt;ul style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positive Feedback:&lt;/strong&gt; Creates hysteresis with two switching thresholds&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RC Timing:&lt;/strong&gt; Capacitor charging/discharging determines oscillation period&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Stable State:&lt;/strong&gt; Circuit continuously switches between two states&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frequency Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Adjust R1 or C1 to change oscillation frequency&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications:&lt;/strong&gt; Clock generation, tone generation, timing circuits, LED flashers&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;"><div class="ch">
    
    <h1>Astable Multivibrator (Relaxation Oscillator) - SPICE Time Domain Analysis</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp:</strong> TL084 (operational amplifier)</li>
            <li><strong>R1:</strong> 1 kΩ (feedback resistor to inverting input)</li>
            <li><strong>R2:</strong> 1 kΩ (positive feedback resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>R3:</strong> 1 kΩ (reference resistor to ground)</li>
            <li><strong>C1:</strong> 1 μF (timing capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>V1:</strong> +10V (positive supply)</li>
            <li><strong>V2:</strong> -10V (negative supply)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Oscillation Frequency Calculation</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        β = R3 / (R2 + R3) = 1k / (1k + 1k) = 0.5<br>
        Threshold voltages: Vth+ = +5V, Vth- = -5V<br>
        T = 2RC × ln((1+β)/(1-β)) = 2 × 1k × 1μF × ln(3) ≈ <strong>2.2 ms</strong><br>
        f = 1/T ≈ <strong>455 Hz</strong>
    </div>

    <h2>Simulation Results</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">

        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Capacitor Voltage V(in) - Blue</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Exponential charging/discharging waveform</li>
                <li>Oscillates between approximately -4V and +4V</li>
                <li>Charges toward +10V when output is HIGH</li>
                <li>Discharges toward -10V when output is LOW</li>
                <li>Switches direction at ±5V thresholds</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Output Voltage V(out) - Red</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Square wave oscillating between +10V and -10V</li>
                <li>Period ≈ 2.2 ms (frequency ≈ 455 Hz)</li>
                <li>50% duty cycle (symmetric oscillation)</li>
                <li>Switches when capacitor voltage reaches thresholds</li>
                <li>Rail-to-rail output swing</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">This circuit is an <strong>Astable Multivibrator</strong> (Relaxation Oscillator) using a TL084 op-amp. The circuit generates continuous oscillation without any external input signal. The capacitor C1 charges and discharges through R1, while the positive feedback network (R2, R3) creates two threshold voltages at ±5V. When the capacitor voltage reaches +5V, the output switches from +10V to -10V, causing the capacitor to discharge. When it reaches -5V, the output switches back to +10V, and the cycle repeats. This creates a self-sustaining oscillation at approximately 455 Hz, producing both a square wave output and a triangular/exponential waveform at the capacitor.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card" style="background-color: #e8f8f5; border-left: 4px solid #1abc9c;">
        <h2 style="color: #16a085;">Operating Principle</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Positive Feedback:</strong> Creates hysteresis with two switching thresholds</li>
            <li><strong>RC Timing:</strong> Capacitor charging/discharging determines oscillation period</li>
            <li><strong>No Stable State:</strong> Circuit continuously switches between two states</li>
            <li><strong>Frequency Control:</strong> Adjust R1 or C1 to change oscillation frequency</li>
            <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Clock generation, tone generation, timing circuits, LED flashers</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

